    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s Frankish empire united much of Western and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-europe">Central Europe</a> and revived the Western imperial title in 800.</li><li>Its scholars copied much of the classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> literature that survives today, in the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-minuscule">Carolingian minuscule</a> script.</li><li>The Frankish custom of dividing realms among sons split it at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a> in 843 and broke it apart for good by 888.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> penny, struck at 240 to the pound, was the basis of the pound-shilling-penny system used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> until 1971.</p></aside>
    </section>

